<title>USA: American Eco sees venture revenues.</title>
<headline>American Eco sees venture revenues.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Eco Corp said it should see third and fourth quarter revenues from the initial contract awarded a venture formed by its MM Industra Ltd subsidiary and Halliburton Co's Brown &amp; Root Energy Services.</p>
<p>American Eco said the venture has been awarded a contract for CDN $13.0 million, the first in a series of fabrication contracts on the Sable Offshore Energy Project.</p>
<p>The first contract awarded, is for the construction of the first of two steel &quot;Jackets&quot; that will support the topside wellhead facilities in the developments' Thebaud and Venture Fields. ((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.))</p>
</text>
